<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani road tankers call off strike.</title>
<headline>Pakistani road tankers call off strike.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's private transporters moving vegetable oils from ports to factories will resume operations from Saturday after calling off a 26-day strike, a transport association spokesman said on Friday.</p>
<p>The Oil Tankers Owners Association spokesman said the strike was called off after the association agreed to follow a queue system to lift vegetable oils instead of a contract system.</p>
<p>The strike cut oil supplies to mills, resulting in lower production of processed edible oils and higher prices in the local markets. -- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
